<title>SINGAPORE: Stamford Tyres 1H profits fall 37 pct.</title>
<headline>Stamford Tyres 1H profits fall 37 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to October 31 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollar unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			1.13	vs	1.79</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	     2.00	vs	3.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			 54.61	vs     46.95</p>
<p>    Interest expense		1.52	vs	1.30</p>
<p>    Depreciation, amortisation  0.54	vs	0.45</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  0.97	vs	2.17</p>
<p>    Tax				 0.71	vs	0.71</p>
<p>    Associates			0.87	vs	0.33</p>
<p>Note -- Investment holdings company Stamford Tyres Corp said it expected its second half performance to improve following its regional drive into ASEAN and Asia Pacific markets.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
